{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a94f256a33c67b66","name":"CloakShape Fighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-a94f256a33c67b66","title":"CloakShape Fighter","revision":18669,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:31:34Z","sha256":"c4de18ff4614df811d83db072296d822f41e50eddbbf3b9c0149b7f6e5d7a012","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18669","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=CloakShape%20Fighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a94f256a33c67b66","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Kuat Systems Engineering CloakShape Fighter is a contemporary of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Z-95 Headhunter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Z-95_Headhunter","referenceId":"reference:c01adb1b99b911a6"},". Originally designed as an atmospheric fighter, the CloakShape has proven to be easily adapted to space conflict, though always as a short-range fighter. Many Jedi used modified CloakShapes in the years before ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", modifying them with enhanced maneuverability and painting them bright white (causing them to be called Whitecloak Fighters). When custom Jedi ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," came into production, this practice ended.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Sales of the CloakShape were initially very good, and vast numbers were manufactured in the first decade of production. When superior designs came into production, Kuat Systems Engineering licensed the design of the CloakShape so other shipyards (usually small planetary businesses) could produce them for local markets. Though overshadowed by later fighters, CloakShapes continue to appear in pirate and local planetary defense groups well into the era of the Galactic Alliance.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Efforts to upgrade CloakShapes so they can compete with more modern ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},", usually by adding shield generators and replacing the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concussion Missiles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concussion_Missiles","referenceId":"reference:c95ee0f6eb24f16e"}," with Fire-Linked ",{"tag":"a","children":["Proton Torpedoes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Proton_Torpedoes","referenceId":"reference:89c41c332c03f2dd"},", inevitable fail or cost so much they aren't economically viable. Still, some modifications have stood the test of time, such as:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["Adding ",{"tag":"a","children":["Maneuvering Jets"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Maneuvering_Jets","referenceId":"reference:23baa546c4100844"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"}," +3, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," +3, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," 15 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"}," 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," 17, +4,800 credits)"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Adding a  ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive Sled"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive_Sled"}," with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Socket"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Socket","referenceId":"reference:b6e7b59b72abbbc5"}," for an ",{"tag":"a","children":["R2-Series Astromech Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/R2-Series_Astromech_Droid","referenceId":"reference:fec1452b3294defc"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," Class 3, 10-Jump Memory, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," +13, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," +13, +19,500 credits)"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The CloakShape depends on durability rather than agility to survive combat. Armed with both ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concussion Missiles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concussion_Missiles","referenceId":"reference:c95ee0f6eb24f16e"},", these ships pack a heavy punch- as long as their payload lasts. The lack of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Shields"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Shields","referenceId":"reference:70740894b304e903"}," limits their ability to survive multiple hits, however. As such, they are most popular with groups that expect to strike larger, lightly armed vessels such as bulk freighters. Some early Rebellion units even successfully took on Imperial ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," with CloakShapes by luring away enemy fighters. This tactic proved extremely expensive in the end, because the CloakShapes that were used to draw off the enemy fighters inevitably suffered heavy losses in dogfighting.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["CloakShape Fighter Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +2; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 14 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 27; +7 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 140; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 10; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 47\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Fly 15 Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Character Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Character_Scale"},"), Fly 4 Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},"); (Maximum Velocity 950 km/h)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Ranged (",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54ff